# cornerdetect

- Label: Corner Detect
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 1 to 1
- Parameters: 5 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/cornerdetect.html
- Summary (EN): Corner Detect analyses a single-channel (mono) layer to locate corner features. Its output is a grayscale layer in which detected corners appear as blobs, usable downstream for example with Points from Blobs. Available since 22.0.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Corner Detect repère les coins d'une couche mono et les restitue en taches lumineuses, exploitables ensuite par exemple avec Points from Blobs.

- Inputs meaning: ["input: a mono layer"]

- Key parameters: ["Type: selects the detection algorithm; one option is Harris Stephens (fast) 1988; other options are not listed on the page", "Neighbors: number of adjacent pixels considered", "Threshold: only values above this level are corner candidates", "K: Harris Stephens sensitivity, valid range 0.04 to 0.06; higher values make the detector less sensitive"]

- Caveats: ["K applies only to Harris Stephens and its valid range is narrow", "The other Type options and tuning guidance for Neighbors and Threshold are not documented", "The input must be mono; the page does not say how other layer types are handled"]

